# hyphaed patch series for --source-mode kernel-org --target 7.1.2 (ordered)
#
# Parallel to patches/series (the Ubuntu/7.0.x default path) — kept separate
# because re-pinning the default series in place would break the proven,
# daily-driver Ubuntu pipeline. Validated 2026-06-25 via `git am --3way` in
# sequence (not just individual `git apply --check`) against a real
# kernel.org v7.1.1 clone.
#
# Dropped vs. the 7.0.x series:
#   0007-xanmod-zen-sched-latency — Its 7.1 replacement candidate (XanMod's
#                            "fair: Set scheduler tunable latencies to
#                            unscaled", origin/7.1 commit bc8670f50cb9)
#                            applies in isolation but CONFLICTS with BORE
#                            (0001) when applied in sequence — BORE rewrites
#                            fair.c's latency mechanism extensively and
#                            supersedes this tunable anyway. Confirmed
#                            CONFLICT via patches/eval.py (2026-06-27).
#
# Re-dropped 2026-07-09 (was re-admitted 2026-06-27, see below):
#   0002-xanmod-bbr3       — CLEAN against the 7.1.1 tree it was validated
#                            on, but the --target default has since moved to
#                            7.1.3 and net/ipv4/tcp_bbr.c diverged enough
#                            upstream between 7.1.1 and 7.1.3 that `git am
#                            --3way` now hits 4 real conflict hunks (one 44
#                            lines) — not a trivial context-line drift.
#                            BBRv3 is TCP congestion control (server network
#                            throughput), not on the critical path for local
#                            AI inference, and hand-resolving unfamiliar
#                            congestion-control C merge conflicts risks
#                            silent correctness bugs. Dropped rather than
#                            patched blind — confirmed CONFLICT via a real
#                            `git am --3way` against a fresh 7.1.3 kernel.org
#                            clone. Re-admit once a 7.1.3-native BBRv3 port
#                            is sourced (check kernel-patches@master again).
#
# Originally re-admitted 2026-06-27 under the assumption BBRv3 is
# upstreamed in mainline 7.1 (it isn't; tcp_bbr.c is still BBRv1 in vanilla
# 7.1.x) — eval.py showed CLEAN against XanMod 7.1.1 and the built 7.1.1
# tree at the time. Sourced as local-file from
# patches/0002-xanmod-bbr3.patch (d83a544c4f01 from XanMod 7.0).
#
# Forward-ported 2026-07-09 (was briefly dropped same day after an initial
# `git am --3way` failure — that failure was a malformed source patch, not
# an unfixable conflict; see below):
#   0018-tkg-pci-acs-override — the vendored 2018-era patch (Mark Weiman fork
#                            of Alex Williamson's original ACS-override) had
#                            hand-edited hunk headers with wrong line counts
#                            (`@@ -5102,6 +5102,7 @@` for a 4-old/5-new body)
#                            and a pre-image blob not in this repo's object
#                            store, so `git am` rejected it outright before
#                            `--3way` ever got a chance to reconcile context
#                            drift. Regenerated cleanly via `git format-patch`
#                            against a real 7.1.3 kernel-org tree (series
#                            0001-0015 applied) — content unchanged from the
#                            original Mark Weiman patch, only hunk
#                            context/placement re-anchored to where
#                            `pci_dev_acs_enabled[]` now lives. Verified
#                            `git am --3way` clean for the full 0001-0018
#                            sequence. Not activated by any preset/cmdline by
#                            default — the boot option `pcie_acs_override=`
#                            just becomes available.
#
# Forward-ported 2026-07-26 (--target 7.1.5):
#   0001-cachyos-bore-scheduler — upstream 7.1.5 refactored util_est:
#                            util_est_update() changed signature to take a
#                            struct sched_entity * and moved out of
#                            dequeue_task_fair() into update_load_avg()
#                            behind a new UPDATE_UTIL_EST flag. BORE's
#                            fair.c hunk carried the old
#                            util_est_update(&rq->cfs, p, ...) call as
#                            leading context, so `git am --3way` failed on
#                            that one hunk (reported misleadingly against
#                            include/linux/sched.h, since this repo's git
#                            baseline has no upstream blobs for --3way to
#                            recover from — see gitops.apply_series). Every
#                            other hunk applied cleanly; BORE's inserted
#                            code has no dependency on util_est. Regenerated
#                            via `git format-patch` against a real 7.1.5
#                            kernel-org tree with the same BORE body as
#                            7.1.4, just re-anchored past the missing
#                            context line. CachyOS kernel-patches@master (21
#                            commits ahead of the local clone) has no 7.1.5
#                            refresh of 0001-bore.patch — re-check there on
#                            the next kernel bump before forward-porting
#                            again by hand.
#
# Sources pinned in patches/VENDOR-kernel-org-7.1.lock.

#
# Runtime verification, 7.1.10, 2026-08-25. First time the series was checked
# against a booted kernel rather than against `git am` exit status. Suite in
# tests/kernel_runtime/; cheap half folded into `python -m hyphaed verify`.
#
# Three patches are NOT what their names suggest, and none of the three is
# broken , they are carried, they apply, and they do not reach the running
# system:
#
#   0002-xanmod-zen-vmscan-swap    Patches vm_swappiness 60 -> 10.
#                            /etc/sysctl.d/99-zzz-greenboost.conf sets 10 as
#                            well, so the live value is identical with or
#                            without the patch and can never testify either
#                            way. Do not cite vm.swappiness as evidence the
#                            series is applied.
#
#   0004-xanmod-zen-max-map-count  Raises DEFAULT_MAX_MAP_COUNT to
#                            INT_MAX-5 (2147483642). MASKED: systemd ships
#                            /usr/lib/sysctl.d/50-default.conf and
#                            55-map-count.conf both setting 1048576, and
#                            userspace runs after the kernel default. The
#                            patched value has never been in effect on this
#                            machine. Left in place rather than dropped ,
#                            1048576 is ample here and removing it would
#                            change nothing , but it is decoration, not a
#                            tuning. Pinned by
#                            verify.check_max_map_count_masked(), which
#                            flips to asserting the patched default if the
#                            distro override ever goes away.
#
#   0005-xanmod-zen-500hz-timer    Adds an HZ_500 Kconfig CHOICE. It does
#                            not select it. The fragments pick HZ_1000, so
#                            the built kernel runs at 1000 Hz. The name
#                            reads like a setting; it is an option.
#
# Two more are inert for a configuration reason rather than a masking one:
#
#   0010 / 0011              Both only change mq-deadline's defaults, and
#                            the NVMe runs 'none'. Proven correct by
#                            switching the scheduler in root-steps.sh and
#                            reading front_merges / write_expire back, then
#                            restoring it.
#
#   0018                     Boot option available, deliberately not on the
#                            cmdline.
#
# And one that cannot be proven on this hardware at all:
#
#   0008-xanmod-blk-wbt-latency    Removes the 75 ms rotational branch so
#                            every queue targets 2 ms. Stock already gives
#                            2 ms to non-rotational queues and this box has
#                            no rotational disk, so the observed value
#                            agrees with the patch and proves nothing. The
#                            test fails deliberately if a rotational queue
#                            ever appears, since that would make it
#                            measurable.
#
# Confirmed genuinely live, with an observable nothing else could produce:
# 0001 (kernel.sched_bore=1), 0003 (vfs_cache_pressure=50, uncontested),
# 0009 (rq_affinity=2 , stock is 1), 0013 (APST 25000), 0014 (THP defrag
# [defer+madvise]), 0015 (KBUILD_EXTMOD guard present in the SHIPPED
# headers package, which is what DKMS builds against), 0019/0020 (all 25
# ioctl checks pass against a real udmabuf-exported dma-buf , first time
# either had ever been exercised).
#
# 0023 was on that list and should not have been. Corrected 2026-08-26: the
# struct_ops type did register, so the "silently never registers" risk noted
# below did not happen , but register_btf_kfunc_id_set() rejected BOTH kfunc
# sets with -EINVAL on every boot, WARNing at kernel/bpf/btf.c:9004, because
# the port carried 6.6.8's BTF_SET8_START (flags 0) where 7.1 wants
# BTF_KFUNCS_START (flags BTF_SET8_KFUNCS). All eight cache_ext kfuncs were
# missing from the verifier's table, so any real eviction policy would have
# been rejected at load while a policy calling none attached happily , which
# is exactly what the runtime probe was. Fixed in the patch; the probe now
# calls one kfunc behind a never-taken branch, and
# tests/test_patch_series.py rejects BTF_SET8_START under patches/custom/.
#
